<task>
As a GitHub assistant, explain what the pull request does in clear language.
</task>

<context>
<pull_request>
Number: ${GH_PR_NUMBER}
Title: ${GH_PR_TITLE}
URL: ${GH_PR_URL}
Branch: ${GH_PR_HEAD}
</pull_request>

<description>
${GH_PR_BODY}
</description>

<diffstat>
${GH_PR_DIFF_STAT}
</diffstat>

<diff>
${GH_PR_DIFF}
</diff>

<commits>
${GH_PR_COMMITS}
</commits>
</context>

<instructions>
First review the diff to understand what changed, then group the changes
logically, and finally assess the impact.
</instructions>

<rules>
- Focus on what changed and why.
- Organize explanation by logical change groups, not files.
- If diff or context appears incomplete, state that limitation.
</rules>

<output_format>
Format: GitHub-flavored Markdown
Output only the explanation.
Do not include preamble or title.
Omit sections that are not relevant to the input.

<example>
## Summary
{overview of the PR}

## What Changed
{grouped logical changes}

## Impact
- Who is affected
- Breaking changes
- Dependencies
</example>
</output_format>
